(DIST/'favicon.svg').write_text('<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 40 40"><rect width="40" height="40" rx="6" fill="#203e35"/><path d="M10 8v23h22M18 8v15h14M26 8v7h6" fill="none" stroke="#fff" stroke-width="2"/></svg>')

overview=f'''<section class="hero-feature"><div class="wrap"><div class="hero-copy"><h1>Project funding.<br>Approval roles.</h1><div><p>Philipp’s project funding, seen through the decisions that released it.</p><p>Follow the proposer, the approving votes and the recipient in three documented cases.</p><a class="hero-read" href="#funding-examples">Explore the decisions {ARROW}</a></div></div><div id="funding-examples">{roles_section()}</div></div></section><div class="wrap"><div class="snapshot"><span><svg viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="10" cy="10" r="7" stroke="currentColor"/><path d="M10 5v5l3 2" stroke="currentColor"/></svg>Records captured October 2026</span><span>Public sources. Dated figures. Evidence you can follow.</span></div><section class="section section-grid" id="briefing"><div class="section-intro"><h2>Four governance concerns to examine</h2><p>The records raise questions about independent approval, technical authority and verification of funded work.</p><div class="context-note"><p>These are governance concerns, not findings of fraud or dishonesty. Payments, voting agreement and timing alone do not establish intent or improper personal gain.</p></div></div><div><article class="finding"><h3>Beneficiaries participated in payment approvals</h3><p>Superbolt records include recipients voting for distributions benefiting themselves. Philipp also voted for Estima’s 45,000-USDC kickoff release.</p><p><strong>What needs clarification:</strong> What independent approval or recusal safeguards applied?</p><p class="note">Other directors approved Estima’s original grant. The Superbolt example received three YES votes; neither is evidence of unilateral approval.</p><a href="/governance/#beneficiary-votes">Read the approval records</a></article><article class="finding"><h3>Technical authority remained after the stated handover dates</h3><p>The preserved audit records continued use of ERIS-held contract powers beyond the published transfer deadlines.</p><p><strong>What needs clarification:</strong> What subsequent decision, if any, authorized that arrangement?</p><p class="note">Philipp cited ongoing maintenance and concerns about the board. No replacement authorization was found in the reviewed record; that does not establish that none exists elsewhere.</p><a href="/governance/#retained-control">Read the terms, operations and response</a></article><article class="finding"><h3>Milestone payments need verifiable acceptance evidence</h3><p>Creda’s 10,000-USDC analytics milestone was paid in January 2026. An October capture of the dedicated analytics page still showed placeholders.</p><p><strong>What needs clarification:</strong> What deliverable was accepted, against which criteria, and where can it be checked?</p><p class="note">A later page capture does not establish that no work occurred. The cited approvals also leave the cost basis and quantified outcomes unclear.</p><a href="/governance/#delivery">Compare the approval, payment and capture</a></article><article class="finding"><h3>A272 proposed concentrating approval power</h3><p>The proposal would have removed a director and reduced the threshold from 75% to 60%. Philipp and MB together could then have approved a decision against the remaining director’s NO vote.</p><p><strong>What needs clarification:</strong> How would that configuration preserve independent scrutiny of beneficiary payments?</p><p class="note"><strong>A272 failed.</strong> The captured board remained four equal seats at 75%. Its timing after the Estima payment does not establish a connection or motive.</p><a href="/governance/#a272">Read the proposal, rules and failed outcome</a></article></div></section>{timeline_section()}<section class="section section-grid funding-context"><div class="section-intro"><h2>Put the funding in context</h2><p>Follow the amounts without confusing a project’s budget with someone’s earnings.</p></div><div><p>The source ledger records <strong>$1,567,716.90</strong> in historical gross funding, receipts and locked allocations across Philipp, ERIS and associated project accounts.</p><p>It combines different categories over different periods. Some receipts are unpriced, and some downstream payments overlap funding already counted.</p><p class="note">This is a historical receipt-value estimate, not personal net profit, a live balance or a measure of loss.</p><a class="button secondary" href="/funding/">Explore the funding {ARROW}</a></div></section><section class="section section-grid"><div class="section-intro"><h2>What holders can ask for</h2><p>Clear records make concrete accountability possible.</p></div><div><article class="finding"><h3>Independent approval</h3><p>Who can approve a beneficiary’s payment without relying on that beneficiary or financially connected parties?</p></article><article class="finding"><h3>Measurable outcomes</h3><p>What was purchased, how was its cost assessed, and what benefit to Terra was required before release?</p></article><article class="finding"><h3>Verifiable control</h3><p>Which contract powers have actually moved, to which wallets, and under what enforceable approval rules?</p></article></div></section></div><section class="takeaway"><div class="wrap"><div><h2>Check the record. Form your own view.</h2><p>Read the evidence, compare the explanations and flag anything that needs correction. The preserved records remain available alongside this shorter account.</p></div><div class="share-control"><button class="button" data-share>Copy link to share {ARROW}</button><p class="share-status" role="status" aria-live="polite"></p></div></div></section>'''
page('Philipp’s project funding and oversight',overview)

index=json.loads((DIST/'record/data/ledger-index.json').read_text())
original=(ROOT/'source-records/original-pages/index.html').read_text()
rows=[]
for row in re.findall(r'<tr id="([^"]+)"[^>]*>(.*?)</tr>',original,re.S):
    key,html=row
    if key not in index:continue
    meta=index[key]
    amt=re.search(r'<td class="amount-col">(.*?)</td>',html,re.S)
    amount=re.sub('<[^>]+>','',amt[1]) if amt else ''
    cat='project' if key.startswith('project-') or key in ['received-1','received-tla-4813','received-4'] else 'overlap' if key.startswith('overlap') else 'other'
    from html import unescape
    amount=unescape(amount)
    label='Project funding' if cat=='project' else 'Already counted upstream' if cat=='overlap' else 'Compensation, fees & other receipts'
    usd=f'${Decimal(meta["usd"]):,.2f}'
    rows.append(f'''<details class="payment" id="{key}" data-ledger="{key}" data-category="{cat}" data-search="{e((meta['title']+' '+amount+' '+label).lower())}"><summary><span><span class="payment-name">{e(meta['title'])}</span><span class="payment-meta">{e(meta['date'])} · {label}</span></span><span class="payment-value">{usd}</span></summary><div class="payment-body"><p><strong>Recorded token amount:</strong> {e(amount)}</p><p>{e(meta['meaning'])}</p>{'<p class="note">Shown for traceability; not added to the total again.</p>' if cat=='overlap' else ''}<div class="receipt-host" aria-live="polite"></div><p><a href="/record/data/ledger-index.json">Receipt index and valuation data</a></p></div></details>''')
funding=head('Follow the funding','Project grants, compensation, fees and other receipts, kept in context. Open a record to inspect its receipts and transaction links.')+f'''<div class="wrap page-content"><div class="funding-total"><h2>Total recorded, counted once</h2><strong>$1,567,716.90</strong></div><p class="note">Historical USD at receipt. Gross funding, receipts and locked allocation across Philipp, ERIS and named project accounts; not personal profit. Superbolt distributions shown below are not added again.</p><form class="toolbar" role="search" onsubmit="return false"><label for="payment-search">Find a record<input id="payment-search" type="search" placeholder="Search projects or payment types"></label><label for="payment-category">Show<select id="payment-category"><option value="">All records</option><option value="project">Project funding</option><option value="other">Compensation, fees &amp; other</option><option value="overlap">Overlapping distributions</option></select></label></form><p id="record-count" class="count" role="status">{len(rows)} of {len(rows)} records</p>{''.join(rows)}<div id="empty-state" class="empty" hidden><p>No matching records. Try a project name or clear the filters.</p><button class="text-button" id="clear-filter">Clear filters</button></div><div class="reading"><h2>Estima: paid and conditional funding</h2><p>The adopted A266 grant was <strong>125,000 USDC</strong>. The earlier 150,000-USDC request was rejected; it is not an additional budget.</p><div class="milestones"><div><strong>45,000 USDC</strong><span>Kickoff · paid 3 October 2026</span></div><div><strong>45,000 USDC</strong><span>Mainnet launch · conditional, unpaid</span></div><div><strong>35,000 USDC</strong><span>Analytics &amp; TLA integration · conditional, unpaid</span></div></div><p>The 45,000-USDC kickoff is already in received funding. The remaining 80,000 USDC was conditional and unclaimed in the saved record; no fixed deadline was captured. Unpaid does not establish overdue.</p><p>A separate proposed 10–20% operator share was discussed. Its adoption and dollar value are not established. Further prediction-market and maturity-market projects were discussed without a separately established funding amount.</p><p class="note">The 8,640-USDC stewardship installment paid on 17 October 2026 is included above. No unpaid balance remains for that action.</p><p><a href="/record/data/estima-project-context.json">Grant scope and proposal links</a> · <a href="/record/data/operator-fee-statement.json">Operator-fee statement</a></p><h2>Amounts kept outside the total</h2><p>Some additional awards, receipts and reference comparisons cannot be added to this subtotal because settlement, valuation or overlap remains unresolved.</p><ul><li><strong>Hydro Votion:</strong> $50,000 reported paid by the funder; the initial $25,000 is part of it. Settlement and overlap need reconciliation.</li><li><strong>Superbolt:</strong> $80,000 of an original $125,000 award reported paid; $45,000 cancelled. Company funding, not a personal $80,000 receipt.</li><li><strong>Migaloo:</strong> 5,000,000 WHALE reportedly awarded; original approval, transfers and realized vesting are unverified.</li><li><strong>TLA incentive-creation fees:</strong> 228 payments totaling 2,280 LUNA, historically valued at $159.95; excluded pending overlap reconciliation.</li><li><strong>Unpriced receipts:</strong> 576 product-fee and 10 incentive/rebase events. Missing prices do not mean zero value.</li><li><strong>OTC reference comparison:</strong> $80,847.41 market-reference difference on 65 USDC-funded trades, not realized profit. Sale prices, fees and financing costs are missing.</li></ul><p><a href="/record/#supporting">Full qualifications and source records for excluded amounts</a></p><h2>How to read the numbers</h2><p>USD values use preserved historical market references, generally the preceding completed hour, or documented redemption references. They estimate value when received, not sale proceeds. USDC uses market prices rather than an assumed $1.</p><p>Totals use unrounded values, so rounded rows can differ by a cent. A transaction can contain several receipt events. Native grant transfers may have a block reference instead of a transaction hash.</p><p>Fee coverage varies by product and account. The ERIS fee row excludes later collector distributions and reserve withdrawals. Some collectors’ ultimate beneficiaries remain unresolved; an ERIS association does not establish personal retention.</p><p class="note">The main receipt register runs through 11 October 2026, with a targeted stewardship update on 17 October. See each row for its own coverage.</p><p><a href="/record/data/fee-reconciliation.json">Fee reconciliation</a> · <a href="/record/#methods">Complete original method</a></p></div>{nextlinks(('/','Back to the briefing'),('/governance/','Next: examine governance '+ARROW))}</div>'''
page('Follow the funding',funding,'/funding/')

governance=head('Who checks the decisions?','Examine three different questions: who approves payments, what completion means, and who retains technical control.')+'''<div class="wrap page-content"><div class="reading"><h2 id="beneficiary-votes">Beneficiary participation in approvals</h2><p>A payment can be formally approved while still raising questions about the independence of that approval. The relevant records identify who proposed, voted and executed, as well as who received funds.</p><h3 id="estima-release">Estima’s kickoff release</h3><p>The other three directors approved the original A266 grant. Philipp then voted YES on A271, which released its 45,000-USDC kickoff payment. The record therefore distinguishes approval of the grant from approval of a payment benefiting his project.</p>'''+evidence('estima-evidence','Open the grant, release votes and payment','<p><a href="/record/evidence/exhibits/legacy/Belege/E05c.json">Preserved grant terms — A266</a><br><a href="/record/evidence/exhibits/legacy/Belege/E05g.json">Preserved release ballots — A271</a><br><a href="/record/evidence/exhibits/legacy/Belege/E05e.json">Preserved 45,000-USDC transfer</a><br><a href="/record/evidence/#delivery">Explanation and original source links</a></p>')+'''<h3>Superbolt distributions</h3><p>In P3, Philipp proposed a 7,500-USDC invoice payment and voted YES; the payment followed the next day. P35 allocated 45,000 USDC to Philipp and three 15,000-USDC amounts. Recorded beneficiary YES votes included Philipp, MB and Rebel; MB executed.</p><p>Participation differs by decision. In P41, Philipp received a payment but had no recorded vote. The record also documents completed Superbolt milestones; beneficiary involvement does not by itself establish that no work was delivered.</p>'''+evidence('superbolt-evidence','Open the Superbolt approval records','<p><a href="/record/evidence/exhibits/legacy/Belege/E10a.json">Preserved payment proposals</a><br><a href="/record/evidence/exhibits/legacy/Belege/E10c.json">Philipp’s signed Superbolt actions</a><br><a href="/record/evidence/exhibits/legacy/Belege/E10h.json">Neutron milestone acceptance</a><br><a href="/record/evidence/#payments">Full beneficiary and approval comparison</a></p>')+'''<h2 id="delivery">Completion, cost and outcomes</h2><p>The cited approvals do not provide an itemized cost basis, independent price comparisons or quantified outcome targets. Accepting a milestone as complete does not answer what it should cost or how much value Terra should receive.</p><h3>The Creda analytics milestone</h3><p>Philipp proposed and voted YES on A215, enabling a 10,000-USDC analytics milestone. The payment was made on 27 January 2026. A preserved capture of the dedicated analytics page on 18 October still displayed placeholders.</p><p>That capture is evidence of the page’s state at that date. It does not establish that every part of Creda was absent or that no development work took place.</p>'''+evidence('creda-evidence','Open the approval, payment and page capture','<p><a href="/record/evidence/exhibits/legacy/Belege/E05b.json">A215 milestone approval</a><br><a href="/record/evidence/exhibits/legacy/Belege/E05f.json">10,000-USDC payment</a><br><a href="/record/evidence/exhibits/legacy/Belege/E07a.txt">18 October analytics page capture</a><br><a href="/record/evidence/#delivery">Original sources and related captures</a></p>')+'''<h2 id="voting">What the voting record shows</h2><p>Across A1–A289, MB voted YES on 251 of the 252 Philipp proposals on which he cast a ballot. The 23 October 2026 capture combines his earlier and current board wallets.</p><p>The one NO was A28, which used the wrong contract. MB voted YES on corrected A29 five minutes and ten seconds later.</p><p>Agreement is observable; motive is not established by a tally. Read the ballots alongside the payment relationships when assessing the independence of oversight.</p><p><a href="/record/evidence/#votes">Voting data, transaction links and audit scope</a></p><h3 id="a272">The failed A272 threshold change</h3><p>A272 proposed removing a director and reducing the approval threshold from 75% to 60%. With three equal seats, Philipp and MB’s two YES votes would have been enough even if the third director voted NO.</p><div class="ballot-grid"><div><h3>Captured configuration</h3><div class="votes" aria-label="Three of four equal seats required, with explicit NO from the fourth"><span class="vote yes"></span><span class="vote yes"></span><span class="vote yes"></span><span class="vote"></span></div><p>Four equal seats · 75% threshold.<br>Two YES votes alone are insufficient against two NO votes.</p></div><div><h3>Proposed in A272 · failed</h3><div class="votes" aria-label="Two of three equal seats would suffice against the third seat’s NO"><span class="vote yes"></span><span class="vote yes"></span><span class="vote"></span></div><p>Three equal seats · 60% threshold.<br>Two YES votes would suffice against one NO.</p></div></div><p><strong>A272 failed.</strong> The captured configuration remained four equal members at 75%. Explicit abstention can affect the denominator; an absent vote is not an abstention. The comparison above assumes the remaining members vote NO.</p>'''+evidence('a272-evidence','Open the proposal, outcome and voting rules','<p><a href="/record/evidence/exhibits/legacy/Belege/E09a.json">A272 submission</a><br><a href="/record/evidence/exhibits/legacy/Belege/E09b.json">A272 ballots</a><br><a href="/record/evidence/exhibits/legacy/Belege/E09c.json">Recorded failed status</a><br><a href="/record/evidence/exhibits/current/board_config.json">Captured voting rules</a><br><a href="/record/evidence/#governance">Context, membership and later proposals</a></p>')+'''<h2 id="retained-control">Technical control is a separate question</h2><p>The TLA launch terms described handing contract administration to Stewardship after one month and configuration ownership after three. The preserved audit found those powers still held through ERIS wallets.</p><p>Using 27 November 2024 as a conservative common cutoff, it identifies <strong>31 privileged operations in 19 successful transactions</strong> across seven of the ten original TLA contracts. These included code replacements, registry changes and incentive restrictions.</p><p>In his public reply of 19 October 2026, Philipp said ERIS continued to develop, maintain and operate the contracts and considered a transfer inappropriate because of concerns about the board. No replacement authorization for the published deadlines was located in the reviewed record.</p><p>That is a bounded finding about the records searched, not proof that an authorization could not exist elsewhere. Board roles, code-migration administration and registry ownership are distinct powers.</p>'''+evidence('control-evidence','Open the terms, response and operation ledger','<p><a href="/record/handover/">Handover terms, provenance and dated transactions</a><br><a href="/record/handover/evidence/operations.json">Full operation ledger and cutoff assumptions</a><br><a href="/record/evidence/#handover">Philipp’s explanation and original links</a><br><a href="/record/evidence/#current">Separate technical powers at 24 October</a></p>')+'''<h2>What remains to be demonstrated</h2><ul><li>A decision process that addresses beneficiaries’ participation and financial relationships.</li><li>A cost basis and measurable outcomes for funded milestones.</li><li>Authorization for retained powers, or executed transfers with each technical role accounted for.</li></ul></div>'''+nextlinks(('/funding/','Back: funding'),('/timeline/','Next: follow the timeline '+ARROW))+'</div>'
page('Who checks the decisions?',governance,'/governance/')

